---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security — Kineti"
  description="How keys are handled, what you log, and what is not yet fully covered."
>
  <section class="border-b border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-16 pb-8 sm:pt-24">
      <h1 class="max-w-3xl text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-4xl">Security</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">How keys are handled, what you log. Copied from <code class="text-accent">SECURITY.md</code> — repo is source of truth.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="flex min-h-[50vh] items-center border-b border-line">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
      <h2 class="text-xs tracking-wide text-muted">How keys are handled</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 max-w-3xl list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted marker:text-accent">
        <li>Keys live in env vars (<code class="text-accent">GEMINI_API_KEY</code>, <code class="text-accent">XAI_API_KEY</code>) or OAuth tokens in <code class="text-accent">~/.kineti/auth/*</code> 0600. Nothing secret is ever logged.</li>
        <li><code class="text-accent">kineti login</code> uses PKCE (RFC 7636 S256), state validated, waits on 127.0.0.1 loopback. Tokens refresh once, then fall back to env key.</li>
        <li>Outbound sends are recorded <em class="text-fg">before</em> they leave (egress firewall), keys redacted, to <code class="text-accent">.kineti/egress.jsonl</code> and surfaced in <code class="text-accent">receipt</code>.</li>
        <li>Daemon socket <code class="text-accent">.kineti/kineti.sock</code> is 0600 same-user only; not a boundary against malware running as your user.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xs tracking-wide text-muted">What you log</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 max-w-3xl list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted marker:text-accent">
        <li>Receipt / journal: spend, fingerprints, gates, DAG heads, egress tags, clean-files counts. Never raw secrets or source contents.</li>
        <li>No telemetry or phone-home on the marketing site. Installer hits <code class="text-accent">github.com/therawlogs/kineti</code> and your CDN; we do not get your source.</li>
        <li>Verify integrity: <code class="text-accent">curl -fsSL https://getkineti.com/install.sh | sh -s v0.2.2</code> then <code class="text-accent">sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS</code> from the release. <code class="text-accent">cargo install kineti</code> now pulls 0.2.2 from crates.io.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xs tracking-wide text-muted">What is in scope</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 max-w-3xl list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted marker:text-accent">
        <li>Path-fence escapes (symlink tricks), prompt-injection → tool execution, hash-chain bypass, spend breaker races, daemon IPC 0600, token theft, worktree teardown path traversal.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Report privately:
        <a href="https://github.com/therawlogs/kineti/security/advisories/new" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent hover:underline">Security Advisories</a> — response within 7 days. No public issues for exploitable findings.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 border-l-2 border-line pl-4">
        <p class="text-sm font-bold text-fg">Honest limits (v0.2.2)</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted marker:text-accent">
          <li><code class="text-accent">bash</code> (via <code class="text-accent">evidence --cmd</code>, <code class="text-accent">wrap</code>, or <code class="text-accent">swarm</code>) runs with your user permissions — no syscall sandbox yet. Safety is <code class="text-accent">[artifacts]</code> scope + <code class="text-accent">ship-check</code>, not the kernel.</li>
          <li>Gateway + <code class="text-accent">swarm</code>/<code class="text-accent">wrap</code> store hashes + counts only; a compromised gateway worker sees prompts in memory while forwarding. <code class="text-accent">verify</code> and <code class="text-accent">ship-check</code> trust local files.</li>
          <li> Tokens on disk (<code class="text-accent">~/.kineti/auth/*</code> 0600, daemon <code class="text-accent">.kineti/kineti.sock</code> 0600) are only as safe as your user account. Network of spawned processes not restricted.</li>
          <li>Treat Kineti as blast-radius reduction and audit infra — not a hard boundary against a fully compromised host.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">Legacy v0.1 swarm details: workers' bash unfenced inside worktrees, quarantine is pattern-matching, same network/token caveats — see <a href="/docs/security" class="text-accent hover:underline">full docs</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted"><code class="text-accent">/.well-known/security.txt</code> · Full doc: <a href="/docs/security" class="text-accent hover:underline">/docs/security</a> · <a href="/pricing" class="text-accent hover:underline">Join waitlist</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
